+# mac2ios
+
+`mac2ios FILE.a` rewrites platform version metadata in thin little-endian Mach-O
+archive members. The default modern platform is iOS (`2`); `-s` selects the iOS
+simulator (`7`). Legacy-only macOS minimum-version commands retain the existing
+conversion to `LC_VERSION_MIN_IPHONEOS`.
+
+When a member contains both a modern build-version command and legacy minimum
+commands, the converter retains the modern command and removes the legacy ones.
+It compacts only the load-command table, updates its header counts, and zeros the
+freed padding. Archive member lengths and section, relocation, and symbol offsets
+remain unchanged. Invalid command bounds fail before that member is written;
+earlier converted members are not rolled back if a later member fails.
+
+Build and run the metadata-only regression tests:
+
+```sh
+make
+make check
+```
+
+Tests cover x86_64 and ARM64 objects, both platform selections, mixed command
+orders, archive layout, payload preservation, malformed input, and idempotence.
+On macOS they also use Apple `nm` and `otool` to read the converted data. No
+Mach-O fixture is linked or executed. Set `MAC2IOS_REAL_OBJECT=/path/to/member.o`
+to include an additional real-member regression.
